    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2Ncux17Yj6ANSAph5xngrN3)_\n\nModelled on Obsidian's [Supercharged Links](https://github.com/mdelobelle/obsidian_supercharged_links).\n\n## What it does\n- **`sp-tag-emoji`** (`libraries/modules/custom/`): `sp-tag-emoji-rules` maps a tag, or a list of tags that must all be present, to `:emoji` and/or `:face` (and `:position` prefix/suffix for links). `sp-tag-emoji-mode` shows the tags of the heading at point, or the file's `#+filetags:`, as emoji in the modeline (or header line), and decorates `id:` links with the emoji and face of the tags of their note, read from the vulpea db. A combination rule uses up its tags, so `(\"@writing\" \"deep\")` replaces the two single emoji. `sp-tag-emoji-check-rules` lists rule tags missing from `org-tag-alist`, so that stays the single tag registry.\n- **`sp-emoji-font`** (`libraries/modules/ui/`): prepends the first installed colour emoji family (Apple Color Emoji, then Noto Color Emoji, …) to the `emoji` fontset. On Linux, `sp-emoji-font-file` or `M-x sp-emoji-font-install` installs an Apple Color Emoji `.ttf` into `~/.local/share/fonts/sp-emoji/`. The font is not bundled (Apple's licence).\n- Literate docs in `docs/tangles/custom/sp-tag-emoji.org` and `docs/tangles/ui/sp-emoji-font.org`; `init.el`, `docs/main.org` and CHANGELOG follow.\n\n## Checked (Emacs 29.3, headless, container)\nBoth docs tangle; the rules, the combo logic, the heading/file/both sources, inheritance, the modeline string, the header-line placement, the link overlays and face (with a fake tag lookup), turning the mode off, and picking the font from a faked font list.\n\n## Not checked\nHow the emoji render in a graphical frame, whether lambda-line prints `global-mode-string` (use `sp-tag-emoji-placement` = `header-line` if not), the vulpea lookup against a real database, and the Linux font install with a real TTF.\nThe Apple `.ttc` shipped with macOS does not work on Linux; a CBDT-format `.ttf` is needed.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01Xrgdre7xkfaqJ3bbVqXTo5)_",
